brms currently does not support common autocorrelation structures such as ARMA in negbinomial models. Maybe R-INLA or glmmTMB does?

Within the brms framework, you may try to use splines or Gaussian processes. If 'time' is your time variable and 'group' is your group variables, if you have multiple time-series per data set, you can add s(time, by = group) or gp(time, by = group) to you model formula. The latter will be rather slow if you have many observations.

Alternatively, you may try the cor_arr correlation structure. Is is similar to cor_ar, but uses the former response values as regressors instead of the residuals.

