From ubafbff7f5abd72d1 at groups.google.com  Wed Apr  4 21:01:01 2018
From: ubafbff7f5abd72d1 at groups.google.com (David Sidhu)
Date: Wed, 04 Apr 2018 21:01:01 +0000
Subject: Coefficient estimates are unstandardized?
Message-ID: <Bp4xAoIq8Fk.lVIlM82wBQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/Bp4xAoIq8Fk/m/lVIlM82wBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Am I correct that the coefficient estimates in the brms output (i.e., the Estimate column) are unstandardized?

I've found some guidelines for setting priors on standardized regression coefficients. Is there a way to adopt this to brms (in which I assume priors are set on unstandardized coefficients)?

From u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com  Wed Apr  4 21:17:20 2018
From: u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com (Paul Buerkner)
Date: Wed, 04 Apr 2018 21:17:20 +0000
Subject: Re: [brms-users] Coefficient estimates are unstandardized?
Message-ID: <Bp4xAoIq8Fk.CPxH8RNBAAAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Bp4xAoIq8Fk.lVIlM82wBQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
References: <Bp4xAoIq8Fk.lVIlM82wBQAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/Bp4xAoIq8Fk/m/CPxH8RNBAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The scale of the coefficients depends on the scale of the variables (i.e. they are unstandardized) as is the case for most other ordinary regression functions.

Thus, If you want your coefficients to be standarized, you have to standardize your variables.

